---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Accessibility skills for Claude
intro: Accessibility skills for Claude
lead: Claude skills for accessible design and code
permalink: /accessibility-skills/
description: A directory of Claude agent skills dedicated to accessibility, covering audits, WCAG, screen reader testing, mobile, design and content, each linked to its source on GitHub.
---
{%- set skills = a11ySkills.skills %}

<p class="lede">A skill is a folder of instructions that teaches Claude how to do one job really well. These are the ones I&rsquo;ve found written for accessibility work.</p>

<p>There are loads of general skill directories, but accessibility skills are scattered throughout them. On this page I&rsquo;ve pulled them into one place.</p>

<p>Being listed here is not a recommendation.</p>

<p>I&rsquo;ve not reviewed these for accuracy, and no skill makes a product accessible on its own. Read the <code>SKILL.md</code> before you install one, and keep testing with real people and real assistive technology.</p>

<form class="skill-filter" role="search" aria-label="Skills" data-skill-filter hidden>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="skill-search">Search skills</label>
    <span class="hint" id="skill-search-hint">For example &ldquo;screen reader&rdquo;, &ldquo;Figma&rdquo; or &ldquo;SwiftUI&rdquo;</span>
    <input type="text" id="skill-search" name="q" aria-describedby="skill-search-hint" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="skill-category">Category</label>
    <select id="skill-category" name="category">
      <option value="">All categories ({{ skills.length }})</option>
      {%- for group in skills | groupby("category") | dictsort %}
      <option value="{{ group[0] }}">{{ group[0] }} ({{ group[1].length }})</option>
      {%- endfor %}
    </select>
  </div>
</form>

<h2 id="skill-list-heading">The skills</h2>
<p class="skill-count" role="status" data-skill-count>{{ skills.length }} skills, most installed first</p>
<p class="skill-empty" data-skill-empty hidden>No skills match that. Try a shorter search, or all categories.</p>

<ul class="skill-list" aria-labelledby="skill-list-heading" data-skill-list>
  {%- for skill in skills %}
  <li data-category="{{ skill.category }}" data-search="{{ skill.description }}">
    <p class="skill-category">{{ skill.category }}</p>
    <h3><a href="{{ skill.url }}">{{ skill.name }}<span class="visually-hidden"> from {{ skill.repo }} on GitHub</span></a></h3>
    <p class="skill-repo" aria-hidden="true">{{ skill.repo }}</p>
    <p>{{ skill.description | firstSentence }}</p>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>Disclaimer</h2>

<p>The skills belong to their authors, under whatever licence each repository carries. If yours is missing, or you would like it removed, <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">email me</a>.</p>

<script src="/js/skills.js" defer></script>
